    <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,2.8rem);">About Travel Antalya</h1>
    <div class="page-body" style="line-height:1.75; font-size:1.02rem;">

<p>Travel Antalya is an independent city guide to Antalya and the Turquoise Coast of southern Turkey. We write for people planning a trip: first-time visitors choosing between Kaleiçi and Lara, families comparing Belek and Kemer, and travellers who want to know what the weather is actually like in a given month.</p>
<h2>What you will find here</h2>
<p><strong>Things to do.</strong> Ancient cities such as Perge, Termessos and Aspendos, beaches, waterfalls, canyons and the old town, each with practical notes on how to get there and when to go.</p>
<p><strong>Places to stay.</strong> Boutique houses inside the Kaleiçi walls, golf resorts in Belek and large all-inclusive hotels along the coast, described by location and style so you can match them to the kind of holiday you want.</p>
<p><strong>Eat &amp; drink.</strong> Restaurants and local dishes worth planning a meal around, from harbour-side seafood to Ottoman-house dining.</p>
<p><strong>Events.</strong> Festivals and concerts with dates, venues and a link to the organiser's own page, so you can confirm details before you buy tickets.</p>
<p><strong>Guides.</strong> Month-by-month weather articles, winter in Antalya, beach guides and hotel-selection advice.</p>
<h2>How we work</h2>
<p>We check dates and facts against official or organiser sources and say plainly when something is unconfirmed. Opening hours, prices and event schedules change, so we point you to the primary source instead of printing numbers that go stale. Read more in our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p>
<p>Some links on this site go to booking partners. If you book through them we may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. This never decides what we write about a place; see the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
<h2>Get in touch</h2>
<p>Spotted an error, want to suggest a place, or run an event in Antalya? Use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>

